docs {
  # Upload Attachment (Protected)
  
  **Method:** `POST`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/attachments/upload`
  **Auth:** Required (Bearer Token)
  
  ## Description
  
  Uploads a file directly through the backend server using `multipart/form-data`. The server inspects the binary content for MIME sniffing, validates the file size against configured limits for the attachment type, extracts dimensions if it is an image, generates a SHA-256 hash, stores the object in storage, and records metadata in PostgreSQL.
  
  ## Request
  
  ### Headers
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`) |
  | `Content-Type` | `string` | Yes | `multipart/form-data` |
  
  ### Form Data
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `file` | `file` | Yes | Binary media file |
  | `type` | `string` | Yes | Attachment type (`PROFILE_IMAGE`, `GROUP_COVER`, `GALLERY_IMAGE`, `EXPENSE_RECEIPT`, `SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT`, `GALLERY_VIDEO`) |
  | `group_id` | `int64` | No | Associated squad/group ID (required when uploading for a group or group gallery) |
  | `expense_id` | `int64` | No | Associated expense ID (required when uploading expense receipts) |
  | `is_public` | `boolean` | No | Whether the file is publicly readable |

  ## Response

  **`201 Created`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "uploader_user_id": 1,
      "group_id": 1,
      "expense_id": null,
      "type": "GALLERY_IMAGE",
      "original_filename": "photo.jpg",
      "file_size_bytes": 1048576,
      "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
      "sha256_hash": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
      "is_public": true,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1080,
      "duration_seconds": null,
      "access_url": "https://storage.example.com/uploads/photo.jpg",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:00:00Z"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  * `400 Bad Request` — Invalid multipart payload or invalid attachment type
  * `401 Unauthorized` — Missing or invalid token
  * `403 Forbidden` — Requester is not a member of the specified group
  * `413 Payload Too Large` — File size exceeds allowed limit for the specified type
  * `415 Unsupported Media Type` — MIME sniffing failed or invalid file format
}
